# Week 11 Update

## Project Topic
For my final project, I plan to analyze my personal tennis match data collected through SwingVision. I want to use data science techniques to better understand patterns in my game and identify areas of strength and weakness.

## Dataset
The dataset consists of exported match files containing information about shots, points, serve direction, rally length, spin type, and match outcomes.

## Initial Goals
Some of the questions I hope to answer include:
- How effective is my first serve compared to my second serve?
- What rally lengths am I most successful in?
- How does my positioning change my success?
- What tactical patterns appear throughout matches?
- What are my biggest errors?

## Current Progress
So far, I have:
- collected and organized multiple match files
- started cleaning and combining datasets
- explored the structure of the shot and point data
- begun planning visualizations and analysis sections

## Challenges
One challenge so far has been understanding how SwingVision structures player information. Different matches label players as either “host” or “guest,” which changes depending on the match setup. Because of this, I need to carefully determine which rows correspond to my own shots and point outcomes before performing analysis.
